# All HIGH CVEs below live in /usr/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/* - npm's
# *own* vendored libraries, from the npm@11 installed in the base image. They
# fire only when npm itself processes attacker-controlled input at build time
# (malicious brace pattern from CLI, hostile registry or WebSocket peer).
# Application code at runtime is unaffected.
#
# Acceptance: the registry's package-signing model + our trusted CI is the real
# defense for those vectors. Refresh when npm bumps its bundle - image is
# rebuilt weekly via the Sunday cron. Never add CRITICAL CVEs here.

CVE-2026-102276  # brace-expansion 5.0.9 - DoS via stack exhaustion from crafted brace patterns
CVE-2026-102278  # brace-expansion 5.0.9 - DoS via uncontrolled recursion in nested brace patterns
CVE-2026-19534   # undici 6.28.0 - DoS via unrequested WebSocket subprotocol
